# Cargo build trees, wherever a `cargo build` was run from: the root ones, and any nested
# copy a misplaced CARGO_TARGET_DIR produces (a whole build tree reached a commit twice
# through a root-anchored pattern - docs/40 §0 and 2026-09-21).
target/
# The 19998 iteration build dir (AGENTS.md live-testing rule) — a whole second cargo
# target tree, thousands of files the Git GUI would otherwise list as pending.
target-test/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# Where production 19999 runs from: scripts/deploy.ps1 copies target/release/swiss.exe here
# so the linker and the daemon never share a file, and the path is stable for PATH and
# autostart (docs/16 §3.3). A build product, never source.
/bin/

# Local gateway state — same set the Node build never commits. All carry real secrets.
gateway.config.json
managed.json
tunnels.json
jobs.json
.env
*.log
master.key

# Stray dev binaries at the repo root (lmg-* are the pre-rename builds still on disk)
/swiss-dev.exe
/swiss.exe
/lmg.exe
/lmg-dev.exe

# Claude Code scratch: agent worktrees, per-machine settings and the rest of its runtime
# tree (skills, rules, checkpoints, registry) — none of it is source. These used to live
# only in .git/info/exclude on the author's machine; shipping them keeps a fresh clone quiet.
/.claude/

# Dev-only npm tooling for the panel home (crates/swiss-panel/panel — sources, emit script
# and the vitest suite; docs/36) — node is a dev dependency, never a cargo build step; its
# install tree stays untracked.
/crates/swiss-panel/panel/node_modules/

# Agent-authored context under .agents is SOURCE now (docs/, skills/, skill-eval/,
# .mcp.json) and ships with the repo. The worktrees/ subtree stays untracked on purpose:
# each is a full checkout of THIS repo (git would nest the repo inside itself) plus its
# own target*/ build trees - ~157 GB of mechanical copies. Their source state travels in
# the diagnosis zip instead, not in git.
/.agents/worktrees/
/conpty_ref.rs
/term-*.png
/job-*.png

# Panel screenshots taken against the operator's real 19999 instance (docs/20 §9 items 3 and
# 6): they show internal hosts, tunnel layouts and live Redis keys. They stay on this machine;
# the docs/20 record lists them as not shipped.
/docs/assets/20/03-tunnels-groups-*.png
/docs/assets/20/06-data-dropdown-*.png
# Same rule, docs/40 second pass: a value read off a live Redis, with the keyspace around it.
/docs/assets/43/redis-utf8-decode.png
# The rest of the credential-shaped strays the seals never cover.
.env.*
*.cast
*.pem
*.kdbx
